Z||000000||CHAD558939||10-08-2001||01:28 AM||||I HAVE AN 88 PONTIAC FIERO GT.AUTOMATIC WITH 52,000 MILES . THE PROBLEM I'M HAVING IS THAT WHEN YOU DRIVE FOR AN HOUR OR SO AND COME TO A STOP THE CAR JERKS AND STALLS . REPLACED THE DISTRIBUTOR AND THE COILS AND SPARK PLUG WIRES. AFTER IT SITS FOR A WHILE IT WILL RUN FINE , ABOUT FIFTEEN MINUTES LATER SAME THING HAPPENS IT STALLS . CAN ANYONE HELP.||||reg||10
Z||000001||ray b||10-08-2001||01:49 AM||||check the throtle position switch on the side of the throtle body clean contacks on plug WD-40 works fine if that don't work clean the inside of the t/body too.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||GarethWright||10-08-2001||03:32 AM||||would a failed torque converter stall the engine, or just make it shudder a lot?<P>Welcome to the Forum!<p>[This message has been edited by GarethWright (edited 10-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroMaster88||10-08-2001||12:31 PM||||Welcome to the Forum.<P>Sounds like a bad torque convertor lock up solenoid.  Those go bad and it feels like a manual trans when you leave it in gear when coming to a stop.  <BR>Hope this helps!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||10-08-2001||12:58 PM||||I second the TCC solenoid. Happened two all of mine. The quick and dirty fix (until you can replace the splenoid) is to unplug the connector from the tranny. (4 pin square connector on the "firewall" side of the tranny.)<BR>Your gas mileage will suffer some, and it will make your tranny run a little hotter, due to the slippage. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
